@startuml validation-hierarchy
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "SF Pro Display"

title clnrm Validation Hierarchy\nWeaver as Source of Truth

package "Level 1: Schema Definition (Highest Authority)" #LightGreen {
    [weaver registry check] as check
    database "registry/*.yaml" as schemas
    note right of check
      **Source of Truth**
      Validates schema syntax
      and structure.

      Exit 0 = schemas valid
      Exit 1 = syntax errors
    end note
}

package "Level 2: Live-Check Capabilities (Infrastructure)" #LightBlue {
    [test_live_check_comprehensive.sh] as tests
    [10 Test Functions] as testfuncs
    note right of tests
      **Infrastructure Validation**
      Proves live-check tooling
      works correctly.

      Tests ALL live-check
      capabilities before
      relying on them.
    end note
}

package "Level 3: Runtime Telemetry Validation (Integration)" #LightYellow {
    [weaver registry live-check] as livecheck
    [OTLP Collector] as otlp
    [clnrm telemetry] as telemetry
    note right of livecheck
      **Runtime Validation**
      Validates actual telemetry
      from running clnrm tests
      against schemas.

      This is THE validation that
      proves features work.
    end note
}

package "Level 4: Traditional Tests (Supporting Evidence)" #LightGray {
    [cargo test --features otel] as cargotests
    [clnrm self-test --suite otel] as selftest
    note right of cargotests
      **Supporting Evidence**
      Traditional tests can have
      false positives.

      ONLY Weaver validation
      proves features work.
    end note
}

' Flow
check --> tests : schemas valid ↓
tests --> livecheck : live-check works ↓
livecheck --> cargotests : runtime validated ↓

' Level 2 details
tests --> testfuncs : runs
testfuncs --> livecheck : validates tool

' Level 3 details
telemetry --> otlp : exports OTLP
otlp --> livecheck : ingests
livecheck --> schemas : validates against

' Level 4 details
cargotests --> telemetry : generates
selftest --> telemetry : generates

' The Critical Path
rectangle "**The Golden Path to Production**" {
    (1) Developer edits schemas
    (1) --> (2) : git commit
    (2) weaver registry check passes
    (2) --> (3) : CI triggered
    (3) Live-Check tests pass
    (3) --> (4) : infrastructure OK
    (4) cargo test generates telemetry
    (4) --> (5) : telemetry exported
    (5) weaver live-check validates
    (5) --> (6) : ✅ VALIDATED
    (6) Deploy to production
}

legend right
  |= Level |= Authority |= Purpose |= Can Have False Positives? |
  | 1 | **HIGHEST** | Schema syntax | **NO** - Syntax is definitive |
  | 2 | **HIGH** | Tool validation | **NO** - Tests tool itself |
  | 3 | **PROOF** | Runtime behavior | **NO** - Validates actual telemetry |
  | 4 | SUPPORTING | Code tests | **YES** - Tests can lie |

  **Key Insight**: Traditional tests (Level 4) can pass
  even when features don't work. Only Weaver validation
  (Levels 1-3) proves runtime behavior matches schemas.

  **This Test Suite (Level 2)**: Validates that the
  live-check tooling works correctly before relying
  on it for Level 3 validation.
endlegend

note bottom
  **Why This Hierarchy Matters**

  Traditional Testing (What We Replace):
    Test passes ✅ → Assume feature works → ❌ FALSE POSITIVE

  clnrm with Weaver:
    Schema validates runtime telemetry ✅ → Feature proven → ✅ TRUE POSITIVE

  **The Meta-Problem**: clnrm eliminates false positives,
  so we can't use methods that produce false positives to validate clnrm.
  We MUST use Weaver schema validation as the source of truth.
end note

@enduml
